                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "238256271",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198104522380",
                            "num_reviews": 46,
                            "playtime_forever": 590,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 590,
                            "last_played": 1792565515
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The third game in the Blackwell series. The story stands on the shoulders of the first two games and we continue to follow Rosa from the first game. It is expected that we are at least aware of what happened in the previous two games, even if we do not need to remember it all in vivid detail to enjoy this story.\r\nThe notes mechanic from Blackwell Legacy is gone and there is more of the \"free text\" input we got a taste of in Blackwell Unbound. I kind of liked the combining notes into clues mechanic in the first game, but I also understand why it was absent here. I personally think and hope those two game mechanics will be able to coexist in the same game in later installments.\r\n\r\nEven with a few plot holes, and an ending that felt a bit rushed compared to the pace set by the rest of the game, this is still the best game in the series so far. The story manages to make the main character Rosa a bit more interesting than she was in the first game. I will surely continue and play the next game in the series now.",
